## Q1

`ScanChildren::stop` (`crates/c3/src/bounded.rs:162`) kills the registered child with `child.kill()`. `kill_tree_by_pid` and `kill_group` run only when the process table cannot be read (`:174`). Otherwise descendants come from `tree_to_reap`, and the loop breaks when a round kills nobody (`:191`), so a grandchild forked after that snapshot is never scanned. A root with `start: None` is skipped (`:123`); `process_start_iso` returns `None` for a zombie, so a shim that has already exited is not swept by pid. A descendant that calls `setsid` (new group and a new parent) matches neither parent pid nor `pgrp == child pid`. I found no signal to a process group other than the child's own, and no kill of a process whose start time is older than the child's. Linux start times are 10 ms, so `still_same` does not separate a pid reused in the same tick; that was not executed.

## Q2

`AKIA` plus 16 letters still matches `aws-key`, before the assignment filter. `ghp_` plus 36 characters still matches `github-token`. A long password under `auth` passes: `is_key_shaped` (`crates/c3/src/pack/redact.rs:145`) rejects whitespace and a single character class, so `auth = "correct horse battery staple"` and `auth = "12345678901234567890"` are kept (`:170`). Any letters-only, one-case value shorter than 24 characters is a dictionary word under every keyword (`:132`), so `password = "hunterhunterhunter"` passes. Packs and `--diff` use the same `scan`, so those values are sent unredacted. `auth = "endpoint"` passes, as intended.

## Q3

Checks run before `ensure`, `git add`, and the commit (`crates/c3/src/finish/mod.rs:251`). A failure returns `CheckFailed` and does not reach them. Each check has a 120 s `within`; `stop` then waits up to 5 s and `child.wait()`, which does not return if the process will not die. A check that backgrounds work and exits 0 is not swept, because the sweep runs only from `stop`. On success, `--skip-checks` is printed and journalled (`:283`). If the config does not parse, skip substitutes an empty list (`:260`) and the line says none are configured.

## Q4

The start folder is worktree index 0 and is refused (`crates/c3/src/setup/branches.rs:1708`). The checkout C3 is running in is refused (`:1710`). Locked and prunable worktrees are refused. The other worktree that has this branch is the one removed, after those checks. Ignored files are absent from `git status --porcelain` (`:1723`); the next call is `git worktree remove` with no `--force` (`:1738`). If `git branch -d` then fails (`:1749`), that worktree is already gone. `--record-unknown` writes only where `is_unknown` is true (`:511`): not merged, and no C3 record. A foreign description is not a C3 record, so a record is prepended and `set_state` keeps the foreign bytes. Both paths refuse when `C3_CHILD` is set.

## Q5

`github_default_branch` stores `gh repo view`'s name for a day (`crates/c3/src/ci_check.rs:303`). `run_gh` does not clear `GH_REPO` (`:329`), so another repository's default branch can be stored for this checkout and used in `gh run list --branch`. The gate file is 16 hex digits of the canonical path (`:404`); two repositories share one only on a hash collision. `gate_record` and `remember_default` are unlocked read-modify-writes and can drop each other's fields. The claim file stays after success; the next UTC day is a new name, so a killed hook blocks only the rest of that day. `gh` stdout and stderr are pipes; the line is a parsed run id plus a name that passed `branch_text_ok`. No raw `gh` text is printed. `gh` was not run.

## Q6

`capped_line` (`crates/c3/src/hook/mod.rs:106`) keeps the start and cuts at character 397, then adds `...`. The scripts match `c3: `, `codex-consult: `, and `CI: ` at the start, keep order, and keep at most 10. The cut does not remove that prefix. Two lines that share those 397 characters become one, and de-duplication drops the second. If nothing matched, the scripts print the first line with no cut of their own.

## Q7

Git accepts a `.git` symlink; `is_git_entry` rejects every link (`crates/c3/src/setup/repo_models.rs:533`). Git rejects an empty `HEAD`; `is_git_dir` only requires a `HEAD` file plus `objects` and `refs` directories (`:576`), and `hook_line` will edit agent files there. `unreadable_stat` (`crates/c3/src/liveness/proc.rs:1609`) returns `Some("")` for every error except a confirmed missing pid, including `PermissionDenied` when the pid is absent. `pid_alive` treats that as alive. A failed read used to be `None` (gone), which was right when the process was already dead.

## Q8

Tests cover a fixture `tree_to_reap`, a shim already visible before the deadline, the claim race, host names, the plain `auth` word, and a hand-built git dir. They do not cover a fork after the snapshot, `setsid`, `start: None`, ignored files on `--close`, `GH_REPO`, a live `hidepid` mount, or `HEAD` contents. CI was not re-run. README, the rest of the doctor parser, and the CLI test bodies were not read.

## Requested checks

RC1. Directory: a temporary folder. Permission: workspace-write. Command: `git init repo && git -C repo commit --allow-empty -m i && git -C repo worktree add ../wt -b merged && git -C repo checkout -B main && git -C repo merge --ff-only merged && printf '*\n' > wt/.gitignore && echo secret > wt/.env && git -C wt status --porcelain && git -C repo worktree remove ../wt; test ! -e wt/.env && echo DELETED`. Observation: `DELETED` confirms finding #3; a refusal or a surviving `.env` clears it. Budget: 1 minute.

RC2. Directory: repository root. Permission: workspace-write. On Unix, run a 1 s `within` whose child is `sh -c 'sleep 30 & exec sleep 5'`, then `pgrep -af sleep`. Observation: a remaining `sleep 30` confirms finding #1. Budget: 2 minutes.

### Findings

- **F46-1** [major] `crates/c3/src/bounded.rs:123`, `crates/c3/src/bounded.rs:174`, `crates/c3/src/bounded.rs:191` - ScanChildren::stop does not reap every descendant of a registered child. Process-group and tree kills run only when the process table cannot be read. When the table is readable, a round that terminates nobody ends the sweep, so a grandchild forked after that snapshot survives; a root whose start time was not recorded is omitted from tree_to_reap; a descendant that has left the process group and been reparented is not selected. Trigger: The deadline fires after the registered child forks, or the child's start time is unknown (it is already a zombie), or a descendant has called setsid. Evidence: read-code: tree_to_reap continues past a root with start None. stop calls kill_tree_by_pid and kill_group only inside if table.is_err(). After terminating victims it breaks when any is false, so an empty first victim list never gets a second snapshot. Verify: On Unix, under within of 1s, run sh -c 'sleep 30 & exec sleep 5' and see whether sleep 30 is still alive when within returns (RC2). Remedy: On Unix, signal the registered child's process group on round 0 even when the table was read; always take one more snapshot after the handles are killed; if start is unknown, still kill by process group or taskkill /T.
- **F46-2** [major] `crates/c3/src/pack/redact.rs:132`, `crates/c3/src/pack/redact.rs:145`, `crates/c3/src/pack/redact.rs:170` - Real secrets now pass the finish gate and pack/--diff redaction, which share scan(). Any letters-only one-case value shorter than 24 characters is ignored under every keyword, including password = "hunterhunterhunter". Under the bare keyword auth, a value is kept unless it is key-shaped, so a multi-word passphrase and a long digit string are kept. AKIA keys and full-length ghp_ tokens still match their own patterns. Trigger: A staged file, pack, or --diff contains password = "hunterhunterhunter" or auth = "correct horse battery staple". Evidence: read-code: is_dictionary_word is letters only, one case, length under 24, and assignment_value_can_be_secret returns false for it under every keyword. For keyword auth it returns is_key_shaped, which rejects whitespace and a single character class. secret_gate scans with redact::scan; reviewed.rs redacts --diff with the same scanner. Verify: Call redact::scan on those three lines and on AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE and a 36-character ghp_ token; the first two assignment lines stay unchanged and the service keys become REDACTED markers. Remedy: Keep the short setting-word exemption only for a single token under auth. Treat any other 8-character-or-longer assignment value, including phrases with spaces, as a secret under auth, password, secret, and token.
- **F46-3** [major] `crates/c3/src/setup/branches.rs:1723`, `crates/c3/src/setup/branches.rs:1738`, `crates/c3/src/setup/branches.rs:1749` - --close treats a worktree as clean when git status --porcelain is empty, which omits ignored files, then runs git worktree remove with no --force. That deletes the worktree, including ignored files such as .env. If git branch -d fails afterwards, the error reports that the worktree was already removed. Trigger: c3 branches --close on a merged branch whose linked worktree contains only ignored files. Evidence: read-code: The cleanliness check is git status --porcelain with no --ignored. On an empty result the code runs git worktree remove with only the path, then git branch -d. The branch-delete failure text includes the already-removed worktree path.; inferred: Git's remove treats ignored files as not dirty and deletes them unless the command is refused. This was not executed here. Verify: RC1: a linked worktree whose only extra file is an ignored .env, then git worktree remove, and see whether the file is gone. Remedy: Refuse when git status --porcelain --ignored=matching is non-empty, and do not call worktree remove until that check passes.
- **F46-4** [major] `crates/c3/src/ci_check.rs:303`, `crates/c3/src/ci_check.rs:329` - The default branch remembered for a day is whatever gh repo view returns. run_gh does not clear GH_REPO, so another repository's default branch is stored under this checkout's gate key and later used for gh run list --branch. The hook line then reports that run as this checkout's default-branch CI. Concurrent gate_record and remember_default can also drop one another's fields. Trigger: GH_REPO names a different repository on the first lookup of the UTC day, or two gate writes overlap. Evidence: read-code: github_default_branch parses defaultBranchRef.name and remember_default writes it for 24 hours. run_gh sets only GH_PROMPT_DISABLED and GH_NO_UPDATE_NOTIFIER. gate_write replaces the whole JSON object from a prior read. Verify: With GH_REPO set to a repository whose default branch is not this repo's, call ci_branch_in twice and read the gate file's default_branch. Remedy: Resolve owner/name from this checkout's GitHub remote and pass gh repo view --repo that name, with GH_REPO removed. Write the gate file under an exclusive lock that merges fields.
- **F46-5** [minor] `crates/c3/src/setup/repo_models.rs:533`, `crates/c3/src/setup/repo_models.rs:576` - The hook's git-directory test disagrees with git in both directions. A .git symlink to a real git dir is rejected. A directory whose HEAD file is empty or garbage, with objects and refs directories, is accepted, and hook_line will run the model repair there. Trigger: The current directory is under a symlink .git, or under a fake .git whose HEAD is not a symref or an object id. Evidence: read-code: is_git_entry returns false when symlink_metadata says the entry is a link. is_git_dir returns true when HEAD is a file and the common directory has objects and refs directories, without reading HEAD. hook_line calls find_repo_root and then refresh_repo_models. Verify: Compare find_repo_root with git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree on a symlink .git and on a directory with an empty HEAD file. Remedy: Accept a .git symlink only when its target is a git dir and the resolved path stays inside the walk. Require HEAD to be a symref or a 40/64-hex object id before treating the directory as a repository.
- **F46-6** [minor] `crates/c3/src/finish/mod.rs:260` - --skip-checks with a config.json that does not parse continues and, on success, says that no checks are configured. The file was unreadable, so that line is false. Trigger: c3 finish --skip-checks when .c3/config.json is not valid JSON or finish_checks is not an array of strings, and a later step succeeds. Evidence: read-code: On skip_checks the code uses configured.unwrap_or_default(), so an Err becomes an empty skipped list. line() then returns the text that none are configured. The non-skip path still refuses with the parse error. Verify: Write a broken .c3/config.json, run c3 finish --skip-checks on a repo with something to commit, and read the printed checks line. Remedy: When skip is set and the file does not parse, print and journal that the file could not be read and that checks were skipped for that reason.
- **F46-7** [note] `crates/c3/src/liveness/proc.rs:1609`, `crates/c3/src/liveness/proc.rs:149` - An unreadable /proc pid is now Some(""), and pid_alive treats that as alive. That includes PermissionDenied for a pid that does not exist, and a NotFound while the /proc/pid directory still exists. The previous failed read was None, meaning gone, which was correct when the process was already dead, and it can now hold a lock or recovery record open. Trigger: process_start_iso fails with an error other than a confirmed missing pid, then a liveness check uses pid_alive or pid_identity. Evidence: read-code: unreadable_stat returns Some("") unless kind is NotFound, the directory is absent, and hidepid is off (or kill -0 prints No such process). pid_alive returns true when the iso is Some and empty. The unit test expects PermissionDenied on pid 4000000000 to be Some(""). Verify: On Linux, point process_start_iso at a pid that is gone and whose stat open returns EACCES, and check pid_identity is Unknown rather than Gone. Remedy: Keep cannot-tell for a directory that exists or for hidepid when kill -0 succeeds. Return None when the directory is absent and the error is PermissionDenied for a pid kill -0 reports as missing.
